            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a snake, then the Arabic for a bear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: جمل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمل — jamal — \"a camel\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "جمل (jamal) is built on the native Arabic root j-m-l, \"a camel\" (Lane). Hebrew gamal is its cousin, and English camel came through Greek kamēlos from a Semitic word of this kind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
